xnu 0089: accept an unsealed root volume on mondrian

With the HFSX test image the mount now succeeds and VFS_ROOT returns a
root vnode; the next check is the sealed-root one. bsd_init() calls
FSIOC_KERNEL_ROOTAUTH on the root vnode and panics with "rootvp not
authenticated after mounting" when it fails (measured 2026-10-23). That
check assumes an Image4 chain of trust; mondrian boots an unsigned
kernel with no AMFI and an HFS root built by tools/mkiosroot.sh, so the
ioctl always fails.

Print the failure and continue, the way the sweet series does in its
0029. This is the bring-up behaviour, not a security model: once the
image is sealed or APFS with a trust cache, the panic comes back.
--- a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
@@ -957,9 +957,22 @@
 		if (require_rootauth) {
 			/* enforce sealedness */
 			int autherr = VNOP_IOCTL(rootvnode, FSIOC_KERNEL_ROOTAUTH, NULL, 0, vfs_context_kernel());
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MONDRIAN)
+			/*
+			 * MONDRIAN has no chain of trust to extend: the kernel it
+			 * boots is unsigned and there is no Image4/AMFI, and its HFS
+			 * root cannot be a sealed volume. Report it instead of
+			 * panicking; the bring-up root is unsealed by design.
+			 */
 			if (autherr) {
+				printf("MONDRAN: root volume is not authenticated "
+				    "(error %d); continuing unsealed\n", autherr);
+			}
+#else
+			if (autherr) {
 				panic("rootvp not authenticated after mounting");
 			}
+#endif
 		}
 	}
 
